0..75 Comment "// Rose trees: a node holds its children, in two forms. Written directly, a"
76..154 Comment "// node holds a `List` of nodes: the list\'s parameter is strictly positive, so"
155..225 Comment "// each child stands below the node and the family declares; a measure"
226..296 Comment "// recurses through the list\'s `map`, which a call instantiates at the"
297..365 Comment "// children\'s stage, and a run passes `map` the children\'s type as a"
366..429 Comment "// code. Written as a block, a node holds a forest and a forest"
430..505 Comment "// is empty or a tree before a forest: the two families name each other, so"
506..579 Comment "// they are one block, admitted as one and sharing one stage; and the two"
580..655 Comment "// measures name each other, so they are one fixpoint over the sum of their"
656..735 Comment "// domains, each measure that fixpoint at its own summand. A measure may take a"
736..810 Comment "// parameter after the tree, and the fixpoint passes it on. A call through"
811..886 Comment "// either stands one stage below the node or forest it was read from (Abel,"
887..966 Comment "// _Termination checking with types_, doi:10.1051/ita:2004015). What the direct"
967..1026 Comment "// form refuses is in `../../pathological/data/rose.gandr`."
1027..1029 Comment "//"
1030..1109 Comment "// - see: #3722 — a measure passes a parameter after the tree to its sibling,"
1110..1161 Comment "//   by which `treeWeight` and `forestWeight` check"
1162..1187 Comment "// - see: #517 — `Bush`"
1188..1214 Comment "// - see: #393 — `nodes`"
1215..1262 Comment "// - see: #452 — `shrub_nodes`, `grown_nodes`"
1264..1336 Comment "// The naturals the measures count in, their addition, and the lists the"
1337..1366 Comment "// direct form nests through."
1367..1373 Keyword "import"
1374..1375 StringLit "\""
1375..1392 StringLit "./data-base.gandr"
1392..1393 StringLit "\""
1393..1394 Other ";"
